A||||9||Fformula88||Gawking at the Fiero||||1||
Z||000000||Fformula88||08-07-2000||11:41 PM||||I know everyone has had a LOT of people staring at your Fiero.  People are always giving mine looks.  I don't drive it on a regular basis due to the high risk area I work, so when I do it surprises me.  Anyway, today I had a guy in a 91 Corvette Convertible drooling over my car at the riverwalk parking lot.  I thought that was really cool, since he owns such a nice sports car and yet he was all interested in my Fiero Formula!||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-08-2000||12:56 AM||||Hellllllllllllllll yeah!!! Great feeling isnt it! I like it when people w/ expensive cars like Vettes admire my Fiero...I have to always say to them "Yeah nice huh! And the best part is, its paid for!!!"..while these guys are paying a car note close to that of rent.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I also like to tell them, "Say thats a nice Vette (or Mustang or whatever) that you've got there...in fact, its as nice as that one over there...and that one over there...and that one over there......"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||nivlek68||08-08-2000||09:31 AM||||its a rush is it not,i like the ones that turn and look over their shoulders(the passengers)i had one yesterday that did that at a stop sign.TWICE and she needs the hood repainted.||||reg||14
Z||000003||b lo 0||08-08-2000||09:43 AM||||Yeah I was at Pep Boys last night and I thought the cashier (a reather attractive lady) was gonna ome home with me!  She just kept staring at that car and she looks at me and goes "I bet it handles great too".  And the driver's side exhaust tip is misaligned, it's missing the wing, and it needs a paint job bad.  Even the guy who parked next to me in the newer RX7 was staring at it.  I love it!<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000004||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||10:34 AM||||  My SE does the same, it stands out pretty easy.  I've had Vette guys, even Street rodders checking it out, and many people spontaneously yell out "Wow, Is that for sale?"  And of course, it gets a lot of attention from ladies.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000005||Philphine||08-08-2000||10:58 AM||||i get looks but i'm beginning to think it's because the car's about 3-4 different colors, with possibly more to come before i can get it painted. the indy scoop seems to draw the most attention.<BR> <BR>actualy lately a few people have yelled out how ugly the car is but the possitive coments still out weight the negative. some people just stare, i don't know what they're thinking. also depends on what part of town i'm in.<P>formula, what city are you talking about that has a river walk?||||reg||1
Z||000006||HugGRRRFiero||08-08-2000||11:26 AM||||   Pay no attention to the negatives Philphine...  Mine was a few colors for a while and got blank stares too.  Many people just can't and don't understand how much time and hard work it takes to restore a car.  Best of Luck with your Fiero!<P>Brent<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif"> <BR> <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fformula88||08-08-2000||05:06 PM||||I alwasy get a kick out of those stares.  The other thing I love is when I take it to the local oil change place.  There are always new kids in there, and they have never seen one before.  They are amazed at the engine in the back!  I think thats awesome... people who don't know the engine is back there. It surprises me, but is also cool!<P>Philphine, I live in the suburbs of Buffalo, NY.  The river walk is along the Niagara River, not far up from Niagara Falls.  I go rollerblading there all the time.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||08-08-2000||08:30 PM||||The Chic-Fil-A drive through girl asked me about the car a few days ago. She was cute so I went back later and some bimbo snickered at it. The Indy roof scoop does look a little strange, but she laughed. Instead of getting mad, I just left them a nice strip of rubber to remember my by.<P>------------------<BR>The slower they think you are, the more suprised they will be when you smoke them.||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||08-09-2000||01:43 AM||||The day after i got my Fiero painted (yellow) I heard some kids say, "WOW, look at that Ferrari!", then them came and asked me if it was mine...I showed them the keys and my drivers licence, they still dont believe its mine.<P>Then when I came back home the next weekend (220 miles away) EVERYBODY was looking at it.  I went to a baseball game and there was a few people just walking circles around it showing it to their kids!  I hope nobody breaks their necks turning to look at it....<P>Its kust amazing how many looks these Fieros get.  How come my '74 Ford F-100 pickup dosent get this many looks???   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||10
